  "summary": "nolimit-agent ships heavily obfuscated modules for SMS/SMTP/SOCKS abuse infrastructure",
  "details": "The package ships a hidden `.ad/` directory containing 40+ heavily obfuscated JavaScript files with hex-mangled identifiers (`_0x...` symbol scheme consistent with javascript-obfuscator string-array + self-defending output). File names disclose the operational purpose of the obfuscated modules: `sms-providers.js`, `phone-validator.js`, `smtp-health-cache.js`, `socks-loader.js`, `web-command.js`, `advanced-evasion.js`, and a large `x0.js`..`xz.js` module set. This composition — bulk SMS provider dispatch, phone-number validation, SMTP-relay health tracking, SOCKS proxy loading, remote command handling, and explicit anti-analysis evasion — is the shape of an SMS/spam/abuse toolkit or a proxy-and-command relay agent, not a legitimate developer library. The obfuscation is applied across every operational module (not just a licensing/DRM shim) and the `.ad/` dot-prefix hides the payload from casual `ls` inspection. Contextual tracing of these modules was withheld by the upstream safety filter, which triggers specifically on operational-malware content — a corroborating signal alongside the uniform critical-severity obfuscation across the entire operational surface. Installing or loading this package delivers author-controlled, deliberately unreadable code that provides no user-visible utility matching its name and whose file-name manifest indicates outbound abuse capability (SMTP relaying, SOCKS tunneling, remote command execution).",
